+# Droidshooter client with Gamira
 
-This is the Unreal Engine 5.1.0 project for the DroidShooter game!
+In `GameLauncher/`, copy `app.ini.sample` to `app.ini`. Set `gamira_url` and
+`platform_url` to the public Gamira API and authentication platform base URLs.
+The platform URL does not include `/api/v1`. Set the executable path for your OS.
+The game client talks directly to Gamira; no frontend proxy or local cluster
+is included or required. Services and game servers are operated separately.
 
-## Local Builds
+Build the client with the upstream Unreal Engine 5 workflow. In `GameLauncher/`,
+run `go build -o launcher .` and start `./launcher` from that directory.
+No admin credentials belong in the client configuration.
 
-## Dedicated Game Server Docker Image
-
-```shell
-docker build . -t droidshooter-server
-```
-
-To run, you will need a copy of Agones [local SDK](https://agones.dev/site/docs/guides/client-sdks/local/) toolkit.
-
-In one shell, start the local testing SDK server:
-
-```shell
-./sdk-server.linux.amd64 --local
-```
-
-Then in another shell:
-
-```shell
-docker run --rm --network=host droidshooter-server:latest
-```
-
-(In non *nix OS's where Docker is not native, you may need to do a slightly different network configuration to get the
-same experience)
-
-You now have a dedicated game server running on 127.0.0.1:7777
-
-## Client building
-
-See the top level [README.md](../README.md#game-client) game client section for full launch instructions.
